; A FALLIBLE HOST CALL CONSUMED ONCE PER ITERATION — ADR 0027, ADR 0040.
;
; The read is a value of lib/result's sum, eliminated by a `case` inside the
; back edge's argument: both outcomes go round, so the `case` counts and the
; `again` jumps. Reduction leaves the host's own shape: Go receives the pair
; with `:=` and tests `err == nil`, while JS and Java assign it from a
; try/catch template and test null, each through its error type's niche
; (oskinds-2026-10-06). Each iteration reads a file that exists (the harness writes case.oro
; beside the binary) or one that does not, so both the value arm and the error
; arm run on every host.
;
;   run n = the number of successful reads among n, alternating = ⌈n/2⌉
;
; windows declares no host call with several results, and `lib/os` has no
; windows file.
; skip: windows
;
; inputs: 0 1 2 7 10
; expect: 0 1 1 4 5

(use os)
(use result)

(sig run ((n (int 0 100))) int)
(def run (n)
  (loop ((k 0) (ok 0))
    (>= k n) ok
    else (again (+ k 1)
                (+ ok (case (os.ReadFile (if (= (% k 2) 0) "case.oro" "missing.txt"))
                        (result.ok src) 1
                        (result.err e)  0)))))
